SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetMapView` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block): it
  takes `center: [lat,lng]` + optional `zoom` (13) / `compact` / `isEmpty` / `emptyMessage` / `children`
  and renders EITHER the empty leaf (`isEmpty` -> `<EmptyState message={emptyMessage} />`) OR a rounded,
  clipped dark `<MapContainer center zoom scrollWheelZoom={!compact} zoomControl={!compact} dragging={!compact}>`
  with a dark `<MapTileLayer>` and the `{children}` overlay slot. There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise
  in the source, so it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch (the host widget that owns the query renders
  those). Per the sibling presentational-primitive precedent (WidgetChartSummary 0002, WidgetComparisonCard
  0003) this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches:
    • empty leaf   (web `isEmpty` -> EmptyState; native "never a bare box" ContentUnavailableView)
    • populated map (web `<MapContainer>{children}`; native MapKit `Map` + content slot)
    • `compact`    (a REAL interaction/controls branch: web `!compact` -> drag/scroll-zoom/controls)
  Inventing loading/error/stale/offline chrome would fabricate states the source does not have, so they are
  intentionally omitted (documented in WidgetMapView.Adapter.swift).

  Native mapping (web Leaflet -> MapKit per ADR-005/009; no Tailwind ports, per Apple HIG):
    • children (ReactNode)              -> generic `@MapContentBuilder Content` slot (+ no-content convenience
                                           via `WidgetMapEmptyContent`, mirroring the web optional children).
    • center [lat,lng]                  -> CLLocationCoordinate2D; sanitized (finite + in-range) in the adapter.
    • zoom (Leaflet level, default 13)  -> MKCoordinateRegion span via pure Web-Mercator metersPerPixel math
                                           (`WidgetMapGeometry.spanMeters`); ~3.9 km square at z13/lat37.8.
    • compact                           -> `MapInteractionModes` ([] vs .all) + compass/scale controls gate.
    • dark MapTileLayer                 -> adaptive `.standard(elevation:.flat, pointsOfInterest:.excludingAll)`
                                           (the web hardcodes dark tiles only because the web app is dark-only;
                                           native supports light+dark via the adaptive P1/S9 tokens — the same
                                           "drop the Tailwind/hex" rule the sibling primitives followed).
    • rounded-lg overflow-hidden        -> clipShape(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: TSRadius.lg)) (matches the
                                           existing native map corner radius in Sources/Components/Maps).
  WidgetMapView is the native peer of the web `MapContainer`-with-children shell; the shared `TSMapView`
  convenience exposes typed arrays (annotations/route/geofences), not a content slot, so the primitive builds
  on MapKit `Map` directly — exactly as the sibling map primitives in Sources/Components/Maps/*.swift do
  (they import MapKit), with `@MapContentBuilder` content (the documented extension point of that layer).

  Files (1060 lines total): WidgetMapView.Adapter(212)/Model(132)/.swift(130)/Views(109)/Previews(79)/
  Tests(107)/AdapterTests(266).swift + WidgetMapView.strings(25).
  Bindings : P1/S8 WidgetMapViewModel @Observable holder (props + projection; NO HTTP in the view; props
             pushed via `.onChange` so a rebind re-renders; camera re-centers on geometry change);
             P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius) — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex;
             P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade (table "WidgetMapView"); P1/S11 view.opened telemetry
             (slug "WidgetMapView", emitted once + idempotent across appear/disappear).
  i18n     : web source has 0 t() keys (anonymous; its only literal "No location data available" is
             reproduced via widgetMapView.empty). Native a11y/HIG additions: widgetMapView.emptyHint,
             widgetMapView.accessibilityLabel. 0 dead keys.
  a11y     : the empty leaf folds icon+message+hint into one combined VoiceOver element; the map canvas is a
             contained element with a spoken label (widgetMapView.accessibilityLabel); decorative pin icon
             hidden; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce-Motion respected (no custom animation introduced).

